  {
    "sha": "061f7855596f16980b038f69a2b4586be8f5a722",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOV4Fa_NoAKDA2MWY3ODU1NTk2ZjE2OTgwYjAzOGY2OWEyYjQ1ODZiZThmNWE3MjI",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Bren Marshall",
        "email": "brenallenmarshall@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-23T00:52:57Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Bren Marshall",
        "email": "brenallenmarshall@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-23T00:52:57Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(ui): do not size the 3D target from a minimized window's layout\n\nA minimized window has no pixels, so egui lays out a default 10000 x 10000\npoint screen. The viewport panel then measured 6078 x 9838 points, and at a\n2.5 pixel ratio fit_target asked wgpu for a 15195 x 24595 texture. wgpu\nanswers a texture past the device limit with a fatal validation error, so\n`camcraft-ui --minimized <project>` stopped with exit code 101 once the\nproject had loaded.\n\n- A frame whose window has no area keeps the last real viewport size.\n- fit_target holds the size to the device's max_texture_dimension_2d, so a\n  very large window cannot reach the same error on a GPU with a small limit.\n\nRefs #3582\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
      "tree": {
        "sha": "12fe5ac364ea9eb6c452003678fe0b8de46f131c",
